    "notes": "Albert governed Hainaut, Holland and Zeeland from 1358 because his elder brother William III of Hainaut was incapacitated. Only after William's death in 1389 did Albert become count in his own right. Albert did not directly succeed Margaret II in 1356. The omitted intermediate ruler was William III of Hainaut / William V of Holland / William I of Bavaria-Straubing (1330–1389), count of Hainaut from 1356, with Albert acting as regent from 1358 until 1389.",
