    "sourceNote": "British Museum Collections Online, William VI, Count of Holland and Hainaut; standard Bavaria-Straubing regnal catalogues.",
    "notes": "William succeeded Albert in 1404 and ruled the linked Hainaut-Holland-Zeeland inheritance until 1417. His only legitimate heiress was Jacqueline of Hainaut. The requested label 'William III of Hainaut (1365–1417)' is incorrect under the standard territorial numbering. The 1365–1417 ruler is William IV of Hainaut, William VI of Holland and William II of Bavaria-Straubing. William III of Hainaut was his uncle, born in 1330 and dead in 1389.",
